ctrl-app-dut (2.3.0-4~) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  [ Keerthi Gowda ]
  * debian/rules: fix shebang and drop the no-op overrides for
      dh_auto_configure/dh_auto_build/dh_auto_clean/dh_install/
      dh_strip/dh_dwz/dh_shlibdeps/dh_fixperms, letting dh_shlibdeps run
      with default debhelper behaviour
  * debian/rules: drop the data/ prefix from override_dh_auto_install's
      cp -a source; dpkg-source strips the orig tarball's sole top-level
      data/ directory on extraction (standard "3.0 (quilt)" behaviour for
      a single-directory tarball), so the installed binaries must be
      copied from ctrl-app-dut/arm64/... directly, matching
      pkg-btftm/pkg-qcom-sensors
  * debian/control: add Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends} to
      the ctrl-app-dut package, which was missing entirely, so the
      restored dh_shlibdeps run actually has somewhere to record the
      runtime library dependencies
  * debian/control: bump Standards-Version to 4.7.4, set Section to
      non-free/utils, drop Priority/Rules-Requires-Root, switch to
      Build-Depends-Arch for the arm64-specific dev dependencies, and
      add Vcs-Browser/Vcs-Git
  * debian/watch: replace upstream.conf with a debian/watch file,
      matching pkg-btftm convention; the real prebuilt tarball
      (ctrl-app-dut_2.3.0_arm64.tar.gz) already carries its version in
      the filename, so no uversionmangle forcing is needed
  * debian/source/options: add extend-diff-ignore for .github and
      .gitignore
  * debian/gbp.conf: add gbp-buildpackage configuration
  * debian/source/lintian-overrides: add overrides for prebuilt-binary
      source package
  * debian/rules: also install the usr/sbin/ctrl_app_dut copy in
      override_dh_auto_install; the upstream payload ships the same
      binary under both usr/bin and usr/sbin, and the sbin copy was
      being silently dropped

